{"content_hash":"88fa1ab8ca53d066a791d2762838e478b9d2ca43cbfba4c8ba71bac6dcf87fc5","event_uuid":"a634576b-3789-4171-b637-34b321e0696b","position":{"commit_sha":"8eb4be1d38b2d9063260dc60a256237f0d0109ac","position":"1787893722869767001-a634576b-3789-4171-b637-34b321e0696b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cc636b8682f395d555809fe6f8f5f8468c4b850ff9ed7cf8f64a297afae05084","event_uuid":"b2eab1d5-591a-4bc1-aa1a-d8d7aa2823d3","position":{"commit_sha":"f268298ab476ecfdb111ec6268c22c65b6bb6029","position":"1787894972654978001-b2eab1d5-591a-4bc1-aa1a-d8d7aa2823d3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"532b021549fc8231c608f19985012502aaf4efcb908f17231af628b22eb46293","event_uuid":"ef207d00-9c09-420d-8917-de4790a64673","position":{"commit_sha":"768c273c0d7e5b9e0202513a7938e134df4c43e0","position":"1787895020665743001-ef207d00-9c09-420d-8917-de4790a64673"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1147303f5345b90b78c84cff91a0ed820a70c0f729c4afbfe7fcc6bc5a3d8277","event_uuid":"817a7f0e-8c50-4a9f-8526-f0bee2a5750b","position":{"commit_sha":"36dd47a1305991dd391a751b98a768765de9a3f8","position":"1787895376405330001-817a7f0e-8c50-4a9f-8526-f0bee2a5750b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"089815688e1bbf420a3e87245b713f6619516ffdca907bf379a59b5213033e2f","event_uuid":"de18a86c-8d2b-4675-bbaa-da3c73206893","position":{"commit_sha":"760b0c6f97729a472f9b2db1e01f6b24135be603","position":"1787896293758104920-de18a86c-8d2b-4675-bbaa-da3c73206893"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787866491109087731,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"180fa21a-d837-4bfc-a6ac-22cc55aa31a9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"},{"link_uuid":"de18a86c-8d2b-4675-bbaa-da3c73206893","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"98b8-2a62-be9f-490e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAn MCP client cannot see CLI stderr, so the cross-session warning must ride in the\n**structured tool response** of single-ticket MCP tools. rebar already carries exactly this\nkind of advisory in structured responses: `WriteAckOut.description_warning`\n(`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:212`, populated via `_ack(..., description_warning=...)` at\n`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:60`). This story mirrors that pattern with a dedicated\ncross-session field on the single-ticket write and read responses, and leaves bulk-read\ntools untouched.\n\nDepends on the detector (`cross_session_warning_for`, sibling story) and the reducer\nclearing.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` field to the response models used by\nsingle-ticket MCP tools: `WriteAckOut` (`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:196`) for single-ticket\nwrites, and `TicketStateOut` (the model `show_ticket` returns, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:221`)\nfor the single-ticket read. Populate it from `cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, ...)` in\nthe corresponding single-ticket handlers in `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` /\n`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` (extend the shared `_ack` helper to accept and thread the value,\nmatching how `description_warning` is threaded). Because the field defaults to `None`, the\n`outputSchema` gains an optional property and existing clients are unaffected (additive,\nback-compatible).\n\n**Compute the warning BEFORE the underlying mutation runs.** The advisory must reflect the\nticket state **at operation time**, so each handler calls `cross_session_warning_for` first\n(reading the live holder), then performs `rebar.<op>(...)`, then attaches the pre-computed\nstring to its response. Reading after the mutation would, for a state-changing op, race the\nvery field (`claimed_session`) the warning is about.\n\nThe single-ticket MCP tools whose response model carries the field via `_ack` /\n`TicketStateOut` are: the read `show_ticket` (`TicketStateOut`) and the writes\n`comment_ticket`, `edit_ticket`, `tag_ticket`, `untag_ticket`, `set_file_impact`,\n`set_verify_commands`, `archive_ticket`, `link_tickets` (primary `id1`), `unlink_tickets`\n(primary `id1`) — all of which build their ack through the shared `_ack` helper.\n\n**`transition_ticket` and `reopen_ticket` are also covered** — they are the core\nsingle-ticket lifecycle mutations, so epic AC3 (\"single-ticket-targeted operations on MCP\")\nrequires them. They return the raw engine result `dict` (`{ticket_id, from, to,\nnewly_unblocked}`) rather than `WriteAckOut`, so the warning rides as an **additive\n`cross_session_warning` key on that dict** (present only when non-`None`; computed before the\ntransition applies). This is additive and back-compatible — existing keys are untouched.\n\nThe bulk read tools — `list_tickets`, `search`, `ready_tickets`, `next_batch` — do **not**\npopulate the field. `claim_ticket` is excluded for the same reason as the CLI story (an\nalready-`in_progress` ticket fails the atomic claim before any warning).\n\n**Accepted scope limits (documented, follow-up filed as `discovered_from` this story).**\n`check_ac` and `quality_check` return `GateResultOut` — they are `READ_ONLY` gate-verdict\ntools, not the mutation the feature targets, and they share one model with unrelated tooling;\n`declare_no_file_impact` returns a bare `\"ok\"` `str` whose schema would have to change\ntype (a breaking, non-additive change). These three are deferred to the follow-up; the CLI\nsurface already warns on the corresponding verbs, so the signal is not lost system-wide.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` — add `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` to\n  `WriteAckOut` and `TicketStateOut`.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` — thread the value through `_ack` and populate it (computed\n  before the mutation) in the single-ticket `WriteAckOut` write handlers; add the additive\n  `cross_session_warning` key to the `transition_ticket` and `reopen_ticket` dict returns.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` — populate it in the `show_ticket` handler.\n- `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` — add the generated note describing the new optional field\n  (the source of truth for `docs/mcp-reference.md`, which a CI stale-doc gate checks).\n- `docs/mcp-reference.md` — document the new optional response field on the single-ticket\n  tools (including the additive dict key on transition/reopen) and the deferred trio.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **contract test** — drive the real MCP handler functions in-process and assert on the\nvalidated response model (test-design §3 \"producer/consumer shape mismatch\": the real\nhandler produces the model through real `model_validate`). Use a real temporary tracker and\nset the acting session via `REBAR_SESSION_ID`.\n\n- With a ticket held by session A and acting session B, call the `show_ticket` handler and a\n  single-ticket write handler (e.g. `comment_ticket`); assert the returned model's\n  `cross_session_warning` is a non-empty string naming holder `A`.\n- With an A-held ticket, call `transition_ticket` as session B (e.g. `in_progress ->\n  blocked`); assert the returned **dict** carries a `cross_session_warning` key naming holder\n  `A`, and that the transition still applied (the mutation is not gated by the warning).\n- Negative control (same session): acting as A, assert `cross_session_warning is None` (model\n  field) and that the `transition_ticket` dict omits the key (or maps it to `None`).\n- Bulk exclusion: the `list_tickets` / `ready_tickets` responses have no populated\n  cross-session field for A's `in_progress` ticket.\n- Unset-id silence: with `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, the single-ticket handlers return\n  `cross_session_warning is None` (and the transition dict omits the key).\n- Schema check: the tool's advertised `outputSchema` includes the optional\n  `cross_session_warning` property (asserted against the generated schema), and a default\n  response (no mismatch) still validates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The `show_ticket` and a single-ticket write handler (`comment_ticket`) return a model\n  whose `cross_session_warning` names holder `A` when acting as session B against an\n  A-held ticket (checked by an in-process MCP contract test under `make test`).\n- [x] `transition_ticket` as session B against an A-held ticket returns a dict carrying a\n  `cross_session_warning` key naming holder `A`, and the transition still applies (checked by\n  an in-process contract test asserting both the key and the post-transition state).\n- [x] Negative control: acting as session A, `cross_session_warning is None` on the model\n  handlers and the `transition_ticket` dict does not carry a non-`None` warning (checked by\n  the same test).\n- [x] `list_tickets` / `ready_tickets` responses do not populate a cross-session warning for\n  A's `in_progress` ticket (checked by a bulk-exclusion assertion).\n- [x] With `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, single-ticket handlers return `cross_session_warning is\n  None` (checked by an unset-id assertion).\n- [x] `WriteAckOut` and `TicketStateOut` `outputSchema` expose the optional\n  `cross_session_warning` property and existing (unset) responses still validate (checked by\n  a schema/model-validation assertion).\n- [x] `docs/mcp-reference.md` documents the field (checked: `grep -n \"cross_session_warning\"\n  docs/mcp-reference.md` matches).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"add optional cross_session_warning field to WriteAckOut and TicketStateOut"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"thread the warning through _ack and populate write handlers + transition/reopen dict key"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"populate cross_session_warning in the show_ticket handler"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"generated note for the new optional field (source of docs/mcp-reference.md)"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"document the optional cross_session_warning response field"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py","reason":"in-process MCP contract oracle: warn/suppress matrix, transition dict-key, bulk exclusion, schema check"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"],["parent","1aca-695f-a0a4-4236"],["relates_to","98b8-2a62-be9f-490e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","parent_status_uuid":"4d608ec3-098d-4697-afd0-a4da7133b1da","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"734d-0998-c47c-48d9","ticket_type":"story","title":"MCP: carry cross_session_warning in single-ticket tool responses","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["192acfa6-1664-4bd5-a28c-b8a093d96df9","2a27b2e6-1b3f-4931-a49a-e443158cd0e4","869e8d3e-7c52-47a5-b483-9eb88a22ae2a","879343cf-ef7d-4f65-b9e1-72b6682426eb","436a6346-1942-4d5d-a72f-4c6defa73292","4d608ec3-098d-4697-afd0-a4da7133b1da","a634576b-3789-4171-b637-34b321e0696b","b2eab1d5-591a-4bc1-aa1a-d8d7aa2823d3","ef207d00-9c09-420d-8917-de4790a64673","817a7f0e-8c50-4a9f-8526-f0bee2a5750b","de18a86c-8d2b-4675-bbaa-da3c73206893"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787896293758104921,"uuid":"abd20c05-9eae-4eb2-a043-4f2d4c335f85"}